  "text": "مفاوضات\n\n nombreux\n\n preferredStyle StringBuilder ממותחדתי\n\n preferredStyleStringBuilder\n\n מכת\n\n preferredStyleStringBuilder\n\n השמים\nTo solve this problem, we need to iterate through all possible values for \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) (where \\(a\\) ranges from 1 to 9 and \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) range from 0 to 9) and check if they meet both conditions:\n\n1. The sum \\(a + b + c\\) is a perfect square.\n2. The number formed by concatenating \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) (i.e., \\(ab\\)) is a divisor of the number formed by concatenating \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) (i.e., \\(bc\\)).\n\nWe'll use a helper function to check if a number is a perfect square. Finally, we'll iterate over all possible values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) and count the number of valid codes.\n\nLet's implement this step by step.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Function to check if a number is a perfect square\r\ndef is_perfect_square(n):\r\n    return int(math.isqrt(n)) ** 2 == n\r\n\r\n# Count the number of valid codes\r\ncount = 0\r\n\r\n# Iterate over all possible values for a, b, and c\r\nfor a in range(1, 10):  # a ranges from 1 to 9\r\n    for b in range(0, 10):  # b ranges from 0 to 9\r\n        for c in range(0, 10):  # c ranges from 0 to 9\r\n            # Check if the sum a + b + c is a perfect square\r\n            if is_perfect_square(a + b + c):\r\n                # Check if the number formed by concatenating a and b is a divisor of the number formed by concatenating b and c\r\n                ab = 10 * a + b\r\n                bc = 10 * b + c\r\n                if ab > 0 and bc > 0 and bc % ab == 0:\r\n                    count += 1\r\n\r\nprint(count)\n```\n```output\n2\n```\nThe number of possible codes is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
